    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:cad8c23d0530c6f0",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "81aaf4d2fa323e784e37e000871f7efb4d84fbb0dc2331960100c80350780eac",
      "text": "After breakfast, you will explore Cusco with an English-speaking guide. First, you will see Qorikancha, the Temple of the Sun, one of the Inca capital's principal sanctuaries. After the Spanish arrived, the Santo Domingo convent was built on its foundations.\n\nThe route then takes you to Qenqo, a ritual centre with rocky passageways, channels and niches; Puca Pucara, a fortified complex beside the road; and Tambomachay, with its system of stone channels and cascading water.\n\nAt Sacsayhuaman, you will see enormous stone blocks fitted together without mortar. The walls run in zigzags, and the slope offers views over Cusco.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to the airport, fly to Lima and transfer to your hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261104-de39b0be5c37",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "Word's Cusco paragraphs omit Qorikancha, Santo Domingo, the breakfast opening and the detailed RU water-channel and dry-stone descriptions; translate the current RU and localize guide language under editorial section 4.1."
      }
    },
